---
import Marketing from "../layouts/Marketing.astro";
export const prerender = true;
---

<Marketing title="Publishing">
  <article class="article">
    <h1>A notebook, not a new workflow.</h1>
    <p>
      The full hosting application is in development. This guide describes the
      approved publishing workflow; the{" "}
      <a href="/sample">public sample reader</a> is available now.
    </p>
    <h2>Bring your vault</h2>
    <p>
      Import a ZIP containing Markdown and supported images or text attachments.
      The initial import limit is 20 MiB compressed. Obsidian configuration,
      plugins, hidden files, and active document formats are excluded.
    </p>
    <h2>Choose what becomes public</h2>
    <p>
      Your original files stay private. Preview the notes and attachments
      selected for a public release. A release becomes public only after
      explicit confirmation.
    </p>
    <h2>Keep your options</h2>
    <p>
      Update a notebook with a new import. Replace a release, unpublish it, or
      export your original Markdown and attachments. Already downloaded copies
      cannot be recalled.
    </p>
    <h2>Know what you use</h2>
    <p>
      The planned dashboard separates hosted storage, public page views, API
      operations, and MCP tool invocations. Estimated traffic is labeled
      separately from exact quota accounting.
    </p>
    <h2>For developers</h2>
    <p>
      Account-owned API keys and explicitly approved MCP agents are part of the
      implementation plan. They are not enabled in this frontend milestone.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/labsbytir/obsidi.xyz/tree/sandbox/openspec/changes/build-obsidi-saas">
        Read the complete product specification
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </article>
</Marketing>
